{
 "design": "For each reference: its 0.5 mm engineering variant (snap0p5), plus each die moved by +0.5 and by -0.5 mm in x, and separately in y. Moves the fixture gate rejects are listed under 'excluded' and are not run. Every call id names its snap0p5 base, so no call can be mistaken for raw.",
 "execution_rules": [
  "Run exactly the listed calls on the named 45 mm fixtures at grid 64; refuse any design whose hash is not listed, and refuse a fixture whose config sha256 differs.",
  "Admit this as its own job: never append these calls to any other job, the gate-zero job included.",
  "One fresh worker per call, reaped after the call; serial at one CPU.",
  "Before each call, stop if cumulative CPU plus one worst-case call would pass the granted cap.",
  "Keep raw outputs and every incomplete or failed outcome; never rerun a completed call.",
  "Report J per call against the base call: a sampled envelope, not a bound."
 ],
